 "confidence": "medium",
 "notes": "15-pin connector (pins 1-15 in a single row), drawn as a wiring diagram with three input strapping options: 600Ω (full connector drawn), 150Ω and 37.5Ω (pins 1-7 only drawn). The drawing names no connector, so it is called P1; view and connector type are not stated. Pins 8 and 9 are drawn but unlabelled (blank, skipped). Note 1 (as drawn): 'DUE TO TRANSFORMER PHASE REVERSAL ON 600Ω STRAPPING, PIN 5 IS CONSIDERED LOW NUMBER, AND PIN 4 IS CONSIDERED HIGH NUMBER. IT IS ADVISABLE TO SLEEVE THE +48V RUN TO PIN 15.' So 600Ω input polarity is 4 = +, 5 = -. For the 150Ω and 37.5Ω strappings (input on 1 and 4) and for the OUTPUT (13/14) no polarity is drawn, so ports use 'a'/'b'. Shield (7) is drawn to the cable shield in all three options. Title block: Ward-Beck Systems Ltd., M124 Connector Wiring, B 124-09-001, drn. C.S. O'Connell, date Aug-68, chkd. initials. Faint scan, rotated 90 degrees; same content as the issue-1 copy; the ISS. box appears empty."
